  </metadata>
  <wpt lat="51.14511264430892" lon="-100.48464917455553">
    <name>Services</name>
    <cmt>caution</cmt>
    <desc>Very limited services for next 130km</desc>
    <sym>Dot</sym>
    <type>danger</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="50.67400515117623" lon="-99.65030504760742">
    <name>Route Alternative</name>
    <cmt>control</cmt>
    <desc>Riders can choose to stay on main road here instead of taking trail option</desc>
    <sym>Dot</sym>
    <type>checkpoint</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="49.97593725725531" lon="-98.28543226737324">
    <name>Few Services</name>
    <cmt>caution</cmt>
    <desc>Limited services until Winnipeg </desc>
    <sym>Dot</sym>
    <type>danger</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="49.39973000000001" lon="-96.23418">
    <name>Route Alternative</name>
    <cmt>control</cmt>
    <desc>Riders can choose to remain on road instead of taking trail option. Trails ahead are mostly easy, fun riding on good singletrack. </desc>
    <sym>Dot</sym>
    <type>checkpoint</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="51.05204458804815" lon="-100.086605400606">
    <name>Route Altnerative</name>
    <cmt>control</cmt>
    <desc>Riders who wish not to ride the Northage trails can turn here to Hwy 10 and continue on this through the park. </desc>
    <sym>Dot</sym>
    <type>checkpoint</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="50.66510536390305" lon="-100.02110708306537">
    <name>Route Alternative</name>
    <cmt>control</cmt>
    <desc>It is also possible to take the Clear Lake Short Trail here into Wasagaming. Mostly great trail but there is one deep water crossing. </desc>
    <sym>Dot</sym>
    <type>checkpoint</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="50.69805383660991" lon="-99.5671367108869">
    <name>Trail Hazards</name>
    <cmt>caution</cmt>
    <desc>There might be some tree-fall and muddy areas on this section of trail. </desc>
    <sym>Dot</sym>
    <type>danger</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="50.683280000000025" lon="-99.4852653818552">
    <name>Route Alternative</name>
    <cmt>control</cmt>
    <desc>Riders can choose to take Hwy 5 south from here to Road 261. Take 261 east to meet up with route. </desc>
    <sym>Dot</sym>
    <type>checkpoint</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="50.04913000000001" lon="-98.00945000000002">
    <name>Route Alternative</name>
    <cmt>control</cmt>
    <desc>If needed, riders can choose to stay on the paved Hwy 26 here and then take road 246 south to rejoin the route. A ride option if dirt roads are muddy.</desc>
    <sym>Dot</sym>
    <type>checkpoint</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="51.1469354062474" lon="-100.4888948956278">
    <name>Route Alternative</name>
    <cmt>control</cmt>
    <desc>If you want some paved riding for next several kilometres you can take Hwy 5 going east and then take road 274 south to meet up with the route. </desc>
    <sym>Dot</sym>
    <type>checkpoint</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="51.65360746007861" lon="-101.5672247302931">
    <name>No Services</name>
    <cmt>caution</cmt>
    <desc>No services until Grandview - 120km from here.</desc>
    <sym>Dot</sym>
    <type>danger</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="50.71170214818301" lon="-100.00639013260172">
    <name>Route Alternative</name>
    <cmt>control</cmt>
    <desc>For a shortcut it is possible to continue south on Hwy 10. </desc>
    <sym>Dot</sym>
    <type>checkpoint</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="50.21423451833734" lon="-98.904872048885">
    <name>Route Alternative</name>
    <cmt>control</cmt>
    <desc>Riders who need a paved riding option can go south on this road to the Hwy 16 (Yellowhead Hwy) and take this main road east. </desc>
    <sym>Dot</sym>
    <type>checkpoint</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="50.62240482876265" lon="-99.46167744398349">
    <name>Route Alternative</name>
    <cmt>control</cmt>
    <desc>Riders can also choose to take this routing via the larger town of Neepawa. </desc>
    <sym>Dot</sym>
    <type>checkpoint</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="50.10777327417474" lon="-98.46872909589801">
    <name>Route Alternative</name>
    <cmt>control</cmt>
    <desc>Another ride option into Portage is to continue east on 227 rd and then take the paved  240 road south into the city. </desc>
    <sym>Dot</sym>
    <type>checkpoint</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="49.664085476741924" lon="-96.6304144197743">
    <name>Route Alternative</name>
    <cmt>control</cmt>
    <desc>Riders who need a paved ride can take road 210 south from there through La Broquerie to meet back up with the route further southeast from here.</desc>
    <sym>Dot</sym>
    <type>checkpoint</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="49.39969514831202" lon="-96.2127773457247">
    <name>Ticks</name>
    <cmt>caution</cmt>
    <desc>Be aware of tick presence in these woods.</desc>
    <sym>Dot</sym>
    <type>danger</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="49.35548531692376" lon="-96.17165325392057">
    <name>Route Option</name>
    <cmt>control</cmt>
    <desc>Possible to take dirt road out of trail system from here.</desc>
    <sym>Dot</sym>
    <type>checkpoint</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="49.311260000000004" lon="-96.14860000000002">
    <name>Route Alternative</name>
    <cmt>control</cmt>
    <desc>Riders who need a paved route from here can take this road south and then Hwy 12 southeast to meet up with the route by Sprague.</desc>
    <sym>Dot</sym>
    <type>checkpoint</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="49.88787628826822" lon="-97.1268382850196">
